                                <enumeratedValue>
                                    <name>1</name>
                                    <description>Multi-processor reception When the data with the multi-processor bit set to 0 is received, the data is not read, and setting the status flags to 1 is disabled. When the data with the multi-processor bit set to 1 is received, the MPIE bit is automatically cleared to 0, and non-multi-processor reception is resumed. If you want to continue receiving operation using the multiprocessor function, set this bit to 1 sufficiently earlier than receiving the STOP bit of the next received frame (consider the synchronization delay time). </description>
